<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco changes bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco changes bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has lifted A-960 bunker fuel prices from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $1 to $103.50 a tonne ($15.89 a barrel) with effect May 8, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-960 from the Red Sea ports of Jeddah and Yanbu is $2.50 higher at $100 a tonne ($15.35).</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from the two Gulf ports is $1 lower at $212 a tonne and unchanged from the Red Sea at $192.50.</p>
</text>
